# Grafdigger's Cage and Serra Paragon's "you may play a land from your graveyard": playing a land is putting it onto the
# battlefield (CR 305.1), and Dryad Arbor in the graveyard is a creature card, which the Cage keeps from entering
# (CR 101.2) - so the Paragon can't play it. Bot1 casts the Cage and the Paragon on turn 1, then Faithless Looting,
# discarding Dryad Arbor and Plains; it is refused the Arbor and plays the Plains from its graveyard by the Paragon.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Grafdigger's Cage
Serra Paragon
Faithless Looting
Dryad Arbor
Plains
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Grafdigger's Cage.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Serra Paragon.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Faithless Looting.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Dryad Arbor; Plains)
? Bot1.Graveyard = Faithless Looting; Plains; Dryad Arbor; Black Lotus
! Bot1.Graveyard.Dryad Arbor.Play
Bot1.Graveyard.Plains.Play

[Expect]
Turn = 1
Bot1.LandsPlayed = 1
Bot1.Battlefield = Grafdigger's Cage; Mox Jet; Mox Pearl; Mox Ruby; Plains; Serra Paragon
Bot1.Graveyard = Faithless Looting; Dryad Arbor; Black Lotus
